{title: Everlasting Life}
{subtitle: John 3:16}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb/Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb/Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [Bb]was wandering in the valley, [Eb/Bb]lost [Bb]and low
Carrying a burden [F7sus4]that I couldn't [Bb]let go
Then I heard a promise [Eb]from an old worn page
[Bb]Words that broke [Gm7]the chains and ope[F7sus4]ned up the [Bb]cage
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For God so loved the [Eb]world
[Gm7]That He gave His only [F7sus4]begot[F]ten Son
[Bb]That whosoever believeth in [Eb]Him
Should not [Gm7]perish, but have [F7sus4]everlast[F]ing [Bb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Mama sang it softly when the night [Eb]was long
[Bb]Grandpa hummed it [F]working, made the wea[Bb]ry strong
Not a single soul [Eb]is standing out of [Gm7]reach
Love so wide and [F]deep that only [Bb]grace can teach
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For God so [Eb]loved the [Gm7]world
That He gave His only [F]begotten Son
[Bb]That whosoever believeth in [Eb]Him
Should [Gm7]not perish, but [F]have everlasting [Bb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Whosoever, that [Eb]means you
Whosoever, that [Gm7]means me
Whosoever, lift [F]your voice
Sing it out and be [Bb]set free
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For God so loved [Eb]the world
[Gm7]That He gave His only [F]begotten Son
[Bb]That whosoever believeth in [Eb]Him
Should not [Gm7]perish, but have [F]everlasting [Bb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Everlasting [Eb]life, everlasting [Gm7]life
John three sixteen, [F]ev[Bb]erlasting [Eb]life
{end_of_verse}

